Too scant the light for my dim eyes;
These dark days gloom my heart and brain.
The roofs are moist with drizzly raia;
On yonder hills a fog-shroud lies;
For summer time I long again.
For bees hum. bird-sonss. that fain
Would hear, dull, lnufied street-soun,ls rise:
These dark days gloom my heart and oraia
The trees seem mutely to complain:
No feathered anorist through them dies;
For summertime 1 long again.
Hark. there's the organ grinders strain;
He hopefully his trade s,in plies
These dark days gloom my heart and brain.
The window flowers peer through the pane,
Pale, and with me they sympathize;
For summer time 1 long again
E'en Fancy fails; her wonders wane
Her scenes now boast no brilliant dyes;
These dark days gloom my heart and brain.
